# Example local npm configuration for the electron app (copy to `.npmrc` only if needed).
# The `electron` package postinstall downloads the Chromium binary separately from npm tarballs.
# Misconfigured mirror URLs are a common cause of: `TypeError: Invalid URL` in got/@electron/get.

# --- Electron binary mirror (optional) ---
# MUST be an absolute URL with scheme (https://). Missing `https://` breaks the downloader.
#
# Typical China mirror:
# electron_mirror=https://npmmirror.com/mirrors/electron/

# npm package registry (optional; lockfile URLs may already point at a mirror)
# registry=https://registry.npmmirror.com/

# Avoid setting these unless you know the exact filenames @electron/get expects:
# electron_custom_dir=
# electron_custom_filename=
